# Docker does not read .gitignore — only this file. Without it, `COPY . .` in the
# builder stage copies .env (live AWS credentials) into an image layer. The final
# stage only copies the binary out, so the keys never reach the runtime image, but
# they persist in the build cache and are pushed when CI uses registry-backed
# caching. A build context is not a private place.

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local build output
bin/

# Not needed to compile; excluded so editing them cannot invalidate the
# compile layer.
*.md
docker-compose.yml
repomix-output.xml
